 "claim": "A Fano atom with a line removed is transparent (proved for every knot space, a connected cubic system with no not-all-equal colouring). Every closed side of an atom's cut accepts exactly one antipodal pair (a point side) or the six other patterns (a line side), by KNOT-COMPOSE A as corrected by NATIVE-PATHS A, so the atom with its closed sides is a signed Fano plane with no colouring; of the 256 sign classes of the Fano plane exactly one, the plain plane, has none. In the Fano plane, removing any line together with any other element leaves that element's three variables free (91 of 91). Hence an atom with any one of its lines removed sends the free relation through every one of its cuts, the same relation whichever line is removed. The knot is needed: with arbitrary relations on an atom's other cuts this holds for every atom with at most one line-type cut, but for only 209 of 1,609 (configuration, cut) pairs with more. Computed on the 191 saved spaces: all 1,014 closed sides are as stated, and 6,058 of 6,058 (atom, cut, removed line) send the free relation.",
